 "jointsSideReason": "facing gate: Left*/Right* joints were placed on the mesh's right/left (Blender -Y forward, left = +X), so the rig read -160/-170 deg though the head faces +Z; labels swapped to the mesh's own sides",
 "sourceMesh": "artifacts/homm3_mesh_surgery/hota_factory_automaton_arm_a1.glb",
 "meshSurgeryReason": "2026-10-11 lane A (user-approved): telescoping arm. arm_telescope_surgery.py cuts the gripper free of the drum plate and parks three nested sleeves inside the drum; idleCycle.rigidParts (wholeIslands) bind each rigid 100% to its own bone, chained Head > ArmSleeve1 > ArmSleeve2 > ArmSleeve3 > ArmGripper, so the AttackFront patch can slide each sleeve out along -Y (each key's delta within the keyTranslations limit) like the DEF's arm. The sleeves are separate parts, so the only seam is the gripper's cut from the plate (no blended weights needed).",
 "glbPatch": {
  "reason": "authenticity: DEF g12 attack - the drill arm (mesh surgery a1: three nested sleeves + gripper on their own bones under Head) telescopes about one body length out of the front drum (f4 half, f5-f7 full) and draws back in (f8-f9), instead of the welded barrel staying put; the sleeves are separate rigid islands, so no weights change. regrid: the sleeve translation channels are 2-key static holds, resampled onto the table's 10-key grid (without it the deltas interpolated away and the arm never extended in game)",
